WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:03.757
Hey, it’s Evan.

00:00:03.849 --> 00:00:05.351
Today I’m answering a question from one of my

00:00:05.736 --> 00:00:09.136
YouTube viewers Tori who commented on my Evernote Tutorial

00:00:09.368 --> 00:00:11.579
“Best Evernote tutorial I have found

00:00:11.579 --> 00:00:14.522
Thank you. (Thank you so much Tori for the kind words)

00:00:14.531 --> 00:00:17.532
Any suggestions for (Middle School or High School)

00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:20.480
students on organizing sections and tabs?”

00:00:20.878 --> 00:00:22.205
This is such a great question.

00:00:22.224 --> 00:00:24.451
Evernote was not around when I was in high school.

00:00:24.503 --> 00:00:25.737
I kind of wish it was

00:00:26.204 --> 00:00:29.837
How I would do it is, so if I’m here, I’m at my Notebooks,

00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:35.523
I would look at creating a new Notebook for each class that I’m taking

00:00:35.523 --> 00:00:39.991
and then a new Note for every individual class

00:00:40.011 --> 00:00:41.805
every individual topic within that class.

00:00:42.207 --> 00:00:42.707
Here’s how I’d do it.

00:00:42.804 --> 00:00:44.329
If I was doing it I would go to my Notebooks

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:46.617
of course I’ve got all of this other stuff happening in my life

00:00:46.659 --> 00:00:48.354
so I’d create a special stack just for it.

00:00:48.477 --> 00:00:50.287
You can’t start with a stack right away

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:52.072
so you start with a Notebook.

00:00:52.072 --> 00:00:53.760
I would say, maybe call this History.

00:00:54.347 --> 00:00:56.299
So this is my Notebook.

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:59.133
I would right click on that and go Add to stack

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:00.771
create a new stack

00:01:00.801 --> 00:01:03.343
and I would call my new stack

00:01:04.053 --> 00:01:05.195
School

00:01:06.285 --> 00:01:08.827
and then I could go down to school

00:01:08.827 --> 00:01:10.087
and I would create a new Notebook

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:14.341
for every subject that I wanted to create notes on.

00:01:14.438 --> 00:01:17.197
So that could be, you know, however many subjects students are taking.

00:01:17.872 --> 00:01:19.243
Within my History one

00:01:19.355 --> 00:01:21.414
so if I’m going to history class every day

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:22.510
or every second day

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.069
whatever it is, I’d create a new Note for every class

00:01:26.147 --> 00:01:28.691
or every main topic within that History class.

00:01:28.691 --> 00:01:29.824
So I remember when I was in high school

00:01:29.939 --> 00:01:33.018
I used to take notes with a pen and paper.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:34.342
I didn’t even have a laptop in my high school.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:40.079
Pen and paper, and at the top of every page what I would write is the date.

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:41.694
So you just start a new page

00:01:41.743 --> 00:01:43.489
so I do the same thing in Evernote

00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:47.493
and I would call it Nov 22

00:01:48.134 --> 00:01:50.996
(and whatever we’re learning, maybe it’s talking about the)

00:01:51.054 --> 00:01:56.008
War of 1812 and then start typing all my notes.

00:01:56.209 --> 00:01:58.020
And I’d have everything I need here

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.441
about the War of 1812 that I’ve learned in that class

00:02:00.471 --> 00:02:03.104
then maybe, next week I’d come to the class

00:02:03.244 --> 00:02:04.548
and we’re talking about something else.

00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:08.852
I would call that Nov 29

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:14.324
– (and we’re learning about) World War II

00:02:15.982 --> 00:02:17.943
and take all my notes and put that in there.

00:02:18.053 --> 00:02:21.049
And then whenever I need to review my notes

00:02:21.168 --> 00:02:24.736
I could quickly find anything I need either by date

00:02:24.916 --> 00:02:27.358
by topic, or I could do a full text search

00:02:27.563 --> 00:02:28.978
and find anything that I wrote about. 


00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:30.096
So that’s how I do it.

00:02:30.139 --> 00:02:32.906
Again, I’m creating a stack that I call School

00:02:33.287 --> 00:02:37.055
I’m creating Notebooks for every subject that I’m taking

00:02:37.217 --> 00:02:39.208
and then I’m creating every note

00:02:39.641 --> 00:02:42.366
New Notes for every day of the class

00:02:42.366 --> 00:02:45.012
and every new piece of information that’s coming

00:02:45.012 --> 00:02:46.584
through me at that class.

00:02:46.612 --> 00:02:48.749
So again, I wish I had this in high school.

00:02:48.749 --> 00:02:50.545
Would’ve been a lot easier to keep track of my notes

00:02:50.582 --> 00:02:52.671
and find the stuff I was looking for.

00:02:53.211 --> 00:02:54.214
But that’s how I’d use it.

00:02:54.688 --> 00:02:55.447
Great question.

00:02:55.539 --> 00:02:57.997
If you have any other thoughts on this

00:02:57.997 --> 00:03:00.490
another question, I can answer for you.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.473
Please feel free to leave it in the comments below.

00:03:02.489 --> 00:03:04.210
If you guys liked the video, give it a thumbs-up.

00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:05.799
But I really do want to hear from you.

00:03:05.859 --> 00:03:07.086
Let me know what you think. Leave a comment.

00:03:07.246 --> 00:03:08.457
If you have a question about Evernote

00:03:08.502 --> 00:03:11.434
and how to use it I’d be happy to make a video response.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.055
Thank you so much and I’ll see you soon.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.000
